st","Альтернатива ngrok","Самостоятельный хостинг","Активная разработка","Подробные спецификации в issues"],"ar":["تم تطويره في Rust","بديل ngrok","المضيف الذاتي","قيد التطوير النشط","مواصفات مفصلة في القضايا"]},"keywords":{"zh":["zgrok开发者","自托管ngrok替代品","Rust开发","如何使用zgrok","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrok安装","zgrok设置指南","ngrok替代品","自托管工具"],"ja":["zgrok開発者","セルフホストngrok代替品","Rust開発","zgrokの使い方","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrokインストール","zgrok設定ガイド","ngrok代替品","セルフホストツール"],"ko":["zgrok 개발자","자체 호스팅 ngrok 대안","러스트 개발","zgrok 사용법","zgrok vs ngrok","zgrok 설치","zgrok 설정 가이드","ngrok 대안","자체 호스팅 도구"],"es":["alternativa a ngrok","herramientas de AI","desarrollo en Rust","cómo usar zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","instalación de zgrok-developer"],"fr":["alternative à ngrok","outils d''Agents d''IA","développement en Rust","comment utiliser zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","installation de zgrok-developer"],"de":["Alternative zu ngrok","KI-Tools","Entwicklung in Rust","wie man zgrok-developer verwendet","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","Installation von zgrok-developer"],"pt":["zgrok-developer","ngrok alternative","ferramenta de desenvolvimento em Rust","self-hosted","como usar zgrok-developer","o que é zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","instalar zgrok-developer"],"ru":["zgrok-developer","ИИ Агенты","альтернатива ngrok","инструмент разработки на Rust","самостоятельный хостинг","как использовать zgrok-developer","что такое zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer vs ngrok","установка zgrok-developer"],"ar":["zgrok-developer","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديل ngrok","أداة تطوير في Rust","المضيف الذاتي","كيفية استخدام zgrok-developer","ما هو zgrok-developer","zgrok-developer مقابل ngrok","تثبيت zgrok-developer"]}},"owner":"copyleftdev","repo":"zgrok","repoPath":"copyleftdev/zgrok","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.903Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"zgrok-developer","description":"Develop zgrok tunnel service following project conventions, issue specs, and Rust best practices. Use when implementing features, fixing bugs, or reviewing code in this repository.","bodyPreview":"# zgrok Developer Skill\n\n## ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENTS\n\n**These are non-negotiable. Violating these is a failure condition.**\n\n### No Tutorial Comments\n\nNEVER add comments explaining what code does. Code must be self-documenting.\n\nAllowed comments:\n- `///` doc comments for public API\n- `// TODO:` or `// FIXME:`\n- `// SAFETY:` for unsafe blocks\n- Brief \"why\" explanations for non-obvious decisions\n\nForbidden:\n- `// Initialize the counter`\n- `// Loop through items`\n- `// Check if value is null`\n- Any co","body":"# zgrok Developer Skill\n\n## ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENTS\n\n**These are non-negotiable. Violating these is a failure condition.**\n\n### No Tutorial Comments\n\nNEVER add comments explaining what code does. Code must be self-documenting.\n\nAllowed comments:\n- `///` doc comments for public API\n- `// TODO:` or `// FIXME:`\n- `// SAFETY:` for unsafe blocks\n- Brief \"why\" explanations for non-obvious decisions\n\nForbidden:\n- `// Initialize the counter`\n- `// Loop through items`\n- `// Check if value is null`\n- Any comment that restates what the code does\n\n### Branch Workflow (Mandatory)\n\nFor EVERY issue:\n\n1. `git checkout main && git pull origin main`\n2. `git checkout -b feat/ZGROK-XXX-description`\n3. Implement all acceptance criteria\n4. `cargo fmt && cargo clippy -- -D warnings && cargo test`\n5. `git add -A && git commit -m \"feat(component): ZGROK-XXX - title\"`\n6. `git push -u origin feat/ZGROK-XXX-description`\n7. `gh pr create --fill`\n8. Self-review the diff\n9. `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch`\n10. `git checkout main && git pull origin main`\n11. Report completion, await next issue\n\n**NEVER leave PRs open. NEVER work multiple issues. NEVER skip steps.**\n\n## Overview\n\nzgrok is a self-hosted ngrok alternative. This skill encodes project-specific knowledge for effective development.\n\n## Issue-Driven Development\n\nAll work traces to issues in `.github/issues/`. Each issue contains:\n\n- **Acceptance Criteria**: Testable Given/When/Then statements\n- **State Machines**: For stateful components (connections, streams)\n- **Technical Context**: Exact crates, files, data structures to use\n- **Dependencies**: What must exist before this can be implemented\n\n### Reading an Issue\n\n```bash\ncat .github/issues/stories/protocol/ZGROK-010-frame-types.json | jq\n```\n\n### Checking Dependencies\n\n```bash\ncat .github/issues/_index.json | jq ''.dependency_graph[\"ZGROK-012\"]''\n```\n\n## Architecture Principles\n\n1. **Async-first**: Everything uses Tokio. No blocking in async context.\n2. **Protocol-agnostic core**: The multiplexer works over any `AsyncRead + AsyncWrite`.\n3. **Graceful degradation**: Connection loss → reconnect, not crash.\n4. **Observable**: Every component emits tracing spans and metrics.\n\n## Code Patterns\n\n### Error Handling\n\n```rust\n// Library crates: use thiserror\n#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]\npub enum ProtocolError {\n    #[error(\"invalid frame type: {0}\")]\n    InvalidFrameType(u8),\n    #[error(\"stream {0} not found\")]\n    StreamNotFound(u32),\n    #[error(\"io error: {0}\")]\n    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),\n}\n\n// Binary crates: use anyhow\nfn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### Tracing\n\n```rust\nuse tracing::{debug, info, instrument, warn};\n\n#[instrument(skip(stream), fields(stream_id = %stream.id()))]\nasync fn handle_stream(stream: Stream) -> Result<(), Error> {\n    info!(\"processing stream\");\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n### State Machines\n\nImplement exactly as specified in issue `state_machine` field:\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\npub enum StreamState {\n    Open,\n    HalfClosedLocal,\n    HalfClosedRemote,\n    Closed,\n}\n\nimpl StreamState {\n    pub fn can_send(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::Open | Self::HalfClosedRemote)\n    }\n    \n    pub fn can_recv(&self) -> bool {\n        matches!(self, Self::Open | Self::HalfClosedLocal)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n1. **Unit tests**: Per-function, alongside code\n2. **Property tests**: Protocol codec with `proptest`\n3. **Integration tests**: Full tunnel flow in `tests/`\n\n```rust\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n    \n    #[test]\n    fn test_frame_roundtrip() {\n        // Maps to AC: Given valid frame, When encoded then decoded, Then equals original\n        let frame = Frame::Data { stream_id: 1, payload: b\"hello\".to_vec() };\n        let encoded = frame.encode();\n        let decoded = Frame::decode(&encoded).unwrap();\n        assert_eq!(frame, decoded);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## File Organization\n\n```\ncrates/\n├── zgrok-protocol/src/\n│   ├── lib.rs          # Public API, re-exports\n│   ├── frame.rs        # Frame types and codec\n│   ├── codec.rs        # Tokio codec impl\n│   ├── mux.rs          # Stream multiplexer\n│   └── error.rs        # Protocol errors\n├── zgrok-agent/src/\n│   ├── main.rs         # CLI entry\n│   ├── cli.rs          # Clap definitions\n│   ├── tunnel.rs       # Connection management\n│   ├── forwarder.rs    # Local HTTP forwarding\n│   └── tui/            # Terminal UI\n└── zgrok-edge/src/\n    ├── main.rs\n    ├── acceptor.rs     # Agent connection handling\n    ├── router.rs       # Subdomain routing\n    └── bridge.rs       # HTTP-to-tunnel bridging\n```\n\n## Commit Convention\n\n```\nfeat(protocol): ZGROK-010 - define frame types and binary format\nfix(agent): ZGROK-033 - handle reconnection edge case\ntest(edge): ZGROK-054 - add agent acceptor integration tests\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:15:36.065Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust Developer Agents needing self-hosted ngrok alternatives with comprehensive code documentation.","zh":"非常适合需要自托管ngrok替代品并具有全面代码文档的Rust开发者代理。","ja":"Rust開発者エージェントが自ホスト型のngrokの代替品を必要とする場合に最適です。包括的なコードドキュメントを提供します。","ko":"자체 호스팅 ngrok 대체품과 포괄적인 코드 문서가 필요한 Rust 개발자 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollo de Rust que necesitan alternativas de ngrok autoalojadas con documentación de código completa.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développement Rust nécessitant des alternatives ngrok auto-hébergées avec une documentation de code complète.","de":"Perfekt für Rust-Entwicklungsagenten, die selbstgehostete ngrok-Alternativen mit umfassender Code-Dokumentation benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvedores Rust que precisam de alternativas de auto-hospedagem do ngrok com documentação de código abrangente.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработчиков Rust, которым необходимы альтернативы ngrok с само-хостингом и полной документацией кода.","ar":"مثالي لعميل مطور الرست الذي يحتاج إلى بدائل ل ngrok ذات استضافة ذاتية مع توثيق شاملة للكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to develop and deploy a self-hosted ngrok alternative in Rust, utilizing public API documentation with /// doc comments, and ensuring code clarity with brief ''why'' explanations for non-obvious decisions, all while adhering to strict commenting standards and utilizing protocols like ngrok''s tunneling protocol.","zh":"赋予代理开发和部署自托管ngrok替代品的能力，利用公共API文档和///文档注释，确保代码清晰度，并使用类似ngrok的隧道协议，同时遵循严格的注释标准。","ja":"エージェントが自ホスト型のngrokの代替品を開発してデプロイできるようにし、公開されたAPIドキュメントと///ドキュメントコメントを使用してコードの明確性を確保し、ngrokのトンネリングプロトコルなどのプロトコルを使用しながら、厳格なコメント規範に従います。","ko":"에이전트가 자체 호스팅 ngrok 대체품을 개발하고 배포할 수 있도록 하며, 공개 API 문서와 /// 문서 주석을 사용하여 코드의 명확성을 보장하고, ngrok의 터널링 프로토콜과 같은 프로토콜을 사용하면서 엄격한 주석 표준을 준수합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes desarrollar y desplegar una alternativa de ngrok autoalojada en Rust, utilizando la documentación de API pública con comentarios /// doc, y garantizando la claridad del código con breves explicaciones de ''por qué'' para decisiones no obvias, todo mientras se adhiere a estrictas normas de comentarios y se utilizan protocolos como el protocolo de túneles de ngrok.","fr":"Permet aux agents de développer et de déployer une alternative ngrok auto-hébergée en Rust, en utilisant la documentation d''API publique avec des commentaires /// doc, et en garantissant la clarté du code avec des explications brèves de ''pourquoi'' pour les décisions non évidentes, le tout en respectant des normes de commentaires strictes et en utilisant des protocoles comme le protocole de tunneling de ngrok.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, eine selbstgehostete ngrok-Alternative in Rust zu entwickeln und bereitzustellen, indem sie die öffentliche API-Dokumentation mit ///-Doc-Kommentaren nutzt und die Klarheit des Codes durch kurze ''Warum''-Erklärungen für nicht offensichtliche Entscheidungen sicherstellt, und zwar unter strikter Einhaltung von Kommentarstandards und unter Verwendung von Protokollen wie dem Tunnel-Protokoll von ngrok.","pt":"Permite que os agentes desenvolvam e implantem uma alternativa de auto-hospedagem do ngrok em Rust, utilizando documentação de API pública com comentários /// doc, e garantindo clareza de código com breves explicações de ''por quê'' para decisões não óbvias, tudo isso seguindo rigorosos padrões de comentários e utilizando protocolos como o protocolo de túnel do ngrok.","ru":"Позволяет агентам разработать и развернуть самохостящую альтернативу ngrok на Rust, используя публичную документацию API с комментариями /// doc, и обеспечивающую ясность кода с краткими объяснениями ''почему'' для неочевидных решений, все это придерживаясь строгих стандартов комментирования и используя протоколы, такие как протокол туннелирования ngrok.","ar":"يمنح العميل تطوير و نشر بديل ل ngrok مع استضافة ذاتية في الرست، باستخدام توثيق API公共 مع تعليقات /// doc، وضمان وضوح الكود مع تفسيرات موجزة لـ ''لماذا'' للقرارات غير الواضحة، مع اتباع معايير تعليق صارمة واستخدام بروتوكولات مثل بروتوكول نفق ngrok."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing a self-hosted ngrok alternative with strict commenting standards","Implementing public API documentation using /// doc comments for clarity","Ensuring code safety with // SAFETY: comments for unsafe blocks","Tracking development progress through issue specs"],"zh":["使用严格的注释标准开发自托管ngrok替代品","使用///文档注释实现公共API文档以提高代码清晰度","使用// SAFETY:注释为不安全代码块确保代码安全","通过问题规格跟踪开发进度"],"ja":["厳格なコメント規範を使用して自ホスト型のngrokの代替品を開発する","///ドキュメントコメントを使用して公開されたAPIドキュメントを実装し、コードの明確性を高める","// SAFETY:注释を使用して不安全なコードブロックの安全性を確保する","問題規格を使用して開発の進捗状況を追跡する"],"ko":["엄격한 주석 표준을 사용하여 자체 호스팅 ngrok 대체품을 개발하는 것","/// 문서 주석을 사용하여 공개 API 문서를 구현하고 코드의 명확성을 높이는 것","// SAFETY: 주석을 사용하여 안전하지 않은 코드 블록의 안전性을 보장하는 것","이슈 규격을 사용하여 개발 진행 상황을 추적하는 것"],"es":["Desarrollar una alternativa de ngrok autoalojada con normas de comentarios estrictas","Implementar la documentación de API pública utilizando comentarios /// doc para la claridad","Garantizar la seguridad del código con comentarios // SAFETY: para bloques no seguros","Seguir el progreso del desarrollo a través de especificaciones de problemas"],"fr":["Développer une alternative ngrok auto-hébergée avec des normes de commentaires strictes","Implémenter la documentation d''API publique en utilisant des commentaires /// doc pour la clarté","Assurer la sécurité du code avec des commentaires // SAFETY: pour les blocs non sécurisés","Suivre la progression du développement via des spécifications de problèmes"],"de":["Eine selbstgehostete ngrok-Alternative mit strengen Kommentarstandards entwickeln","Die öffentliche API-Dokumentation mit ///-Doc-Kommentaren für Klarheit implementieren","Die Sicherheit des Codes mit // SAFETY:-Kommentaren für unsichere Blöcke gewährleisten","Den Entwicklungsfortschritt über Problemspezifikationen verfolgen"],"pt":["Desenvolver uma alternativa de auto-hospedagem do ngrok com padrões de comentários rigorosos","Implementar documentação de API pública usando comentários /// doc para clareza","Garantir segurança de código com comentários // SAFETY: para blocos não seguros","Acompanhar o progresso do desenvolvimento por meio de especificações de problemas"],"ru":["Разработать самохостящую альтернативу ngrok с строгими стандартами комментирования","Реализовать публичную документацию API с помощью комментариев /// doc для ясности","Обеспечить безопасность кода с помощью комментариев // SAFETY: для небезопасных блоков","Отслеживать прогресс разработки через спецификации проблем"],"ar":["تطوير بديل ل ngrok مع استضافة ذاتية و معايير تعليق صارمة","تنفيذ توثيق API公共 باستخدام تعليقات /// doc للوضوح","ضمان سلامة الكود مع تعليقات // SAFETY: للأجزاء غير الآمنة","تتبع تقدم التطوير من خلال مواصفات المشاكل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust development environment","Adherence to strict commenting standards, forbidding tutorial comments","Development in progress, subject to change based on issue specs"],"zh":["需要Rust开发环境","遵循严格的注释标准，禁止教程注释","开发正在进行中，可能根据问题规格进行更改"],"ja":["Rust開発環境が必要","厳格なコメント規範に従い、チュートリアルコメントを禁止","開発中であり、問題規格に基づいて変更される可能性がある"],"ko":["Rust 개발 환경이 필요합니다","엄격한 주석 표준을 준수하고, 튜토리얼 주석을 금지합니다","개발이 진행 중이며, 이슈 규격에 따라 변경될 수 있습니다"],"es":["Requiere un entorno de desarrollo de Rust","Adhesión a normas de comentarios estrictas, que prohíben comentarios de tutoriales","Desarrollo en progreso, sujeto a cambios basados en especificaciones de problemas"],"fr":["Nécessite un environnement de développement Rust","Adhésion à des normes de commentaires strictes, interdisant les commentaires de tutoriels","Développement en cours, susceptible d''être modifié en fonction des spécifications de problèmes"],"de":["Benötigt eine Rust-Entwicklungsumgebung","Einhalten von strengen Kommentarstandards, die Tutorial-Kommentare verbieten","Entwicklung im Gange, Änderungen basierend auf Problemspezifikationen vorbehalten"],"pt":["Requer um ambiente de desenvolvimento Rust","Adesão a padrões de comentários rigorosos, proibindo comentários de tutorial","Desenvolvimento em andamento, sujeito a alterações com base em especificações de problemas"],"ru":["Требует среды разработки Rust","Соблюдение строгих стандартов комментирования, запрещающих комментарии-уроки","Разработка в процесс